<title>USA: USDA cuts $5 million from West Caribbean GSM-102.</title>
<headline>USDA cuts $5 million from West Caribbean GSM-102.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Tuesday said it decreased by $5 million the allocation of credit guarantees available for sales of U.S. farm products to the West Caribbean countries of Jamaica and Haiti under a Commodity Credit Corp program for fiscal 1997.</p>
<p>USDA said that the decrease lowers the CCC's Export Credit Guarantee Program (GSM-102) for the West Caribbean Region to $35 million.</p>
<p>All other terms and conditions remain the same, USDA said.</p>
</text>
